Z||000002||Haze_Performance||11-24-2001||02:23 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Oreif:<BR><B>These are $279 From RS Motorsports. Souldn't be too hard to adapt a single light unless you like the twin lights.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Yikes!!! $279.. I saw someone here (some time ago) did it themselves. (very cheap)Some how they limited the headlight travel without damaging the motor. I tried a search but no luck... (I know most people don't like either but, I'm thinking about the 2 light setup. That 4 light is awful)<P>Thanks Oreif..   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR><p>[This message has been edited by Haze_Performance (edited 11-24-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000003||artherd||11-24-2001||03:14 AM||||87-88 (Newer design) headlight motors can be made to STOP anywhere you like!  <P>Just build a new angle-plate (to compensate for their now screwey lamp angle) and enjoy!<P><BR>Best!<BR>Ben<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000004||Haze_Performance||11-24-2001||03:20 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by artherd:<BR><B>87-88 (Newer design) headlight motors can be made to STOP anywhere you like!  <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>How do I stop them from going all the way up? <P>||||reg||5
Z||000005||jch82||11-24-2001||03:20 AM||||How do you limit the travel of the newer headlight motors???? What kind of stop do you use?? I'm really interested in 1FST2M6's setup. Those circular headlights are awesome and they stick up just enough but not to high! Anybody got info on his headlight setup??<P>Josh  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jch82_2.jpg"> ||||reg||5
Z||000006||cadaver||11-24-2001||02:42 PM||||You can also limit the early motors. They have the HTS switch. Which stands for High Torque Switch. Which opens the contacts when the motor is pushing against the stop. Just undo the lifting mechanism and prop the light to the desired position and make a stop or maybe a new shorter lifting arm. I was going to do a slim pop up design with the lights I use but I dont have any headlight assemblies to play with since I made the flush sets.||||reg||1
Z||000007||SKIDMARK||11-24-2001||03:08 PM||||I believe someone sells a kit to do this to your headlights. I've seen a couple of low profile light kits on Ebay but can't seem to find them now.<BR> In any case, because the headlight motors work on torque limit switches, you can change the angle plate or relocate the stop for the up position without any damage or mods to the motor. The problem I see would be getting the headlight to aim properly at the reduced height. It does look pretty nice and I think will be one mod I will consider on my SE.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Haze_Performance||11-24-2001||05:06 PM||||Thank you for the info guys... Just what I was looking for..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||14
